==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sh}} {{term|rakija|lang=sh}}/{{term|sc=Cyrl|ракија|lang=sh}}, from {{etyl|tr}}, probably from {{etyl|ar}} {{term|sc=Arab|عرق|tr='araq||[[sweat]] or [[wine]]|lang=ar}} (as the rakija or wine vapor drops are similar to drops of sweat). Exact etymology is hard to pinpoint as this word (or a variant of it) is found throughout the [[Balkans]], the [[Mediterranean]] and the [[Middle East]].

===Pronunciation===
* ra-khy-ya

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# A strong [[distilled]] [[alcohol|alcoholic]] [[beverage]] made from various fruits. "Rakija" is the general name for drinks of this type. In English, the closest equivalents are [[whiskey]] and [[brandy]]. Different types of rakijas exist across the Balkans and the Mediterranean. One of them is the [[slivovitz]], the national drink of [[Serbia]].

